    "q-114024": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114024",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $2{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{2}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-114024-a",
